Next, it uses `tryCatch()` to handle potential errors when converting `x` to numeric. If there are no errors (i.e., all elements can be converted), then `as.numeric()` returns the original `x` with all non-NA elements converted to numeric. Otherwise, it returns `FALSE`.

Finally, it splits the resulting `as.numeric()` object into a list of character vectors using `strsplit()` and converts each element back to numeric using `read.table()`. It then extracts the first column of this list using `lapply()` and `unlist()`. If all non-NA elements have been successfully converted to numeric, then `any()` will return `FALSE` for this list, indicating that all elements are numeric. This result is returned by the function.

